   a. src/lib/analytics.ts: make initAnalytics() return immediately (first line
      `return; // analytics disabled for internal build`). This stops PostHog entirely,
      including email identify. Show me the git diff.
   b. Confirm electron/cua.mjs still forces CUA_DRIVER_RS_TELEMETRY_ENABLED=0.
   c. The bundled Cua driver also checks GitHub for updates. Set
      CUA_DRIVER_RS_UPDATE_CHECK=false (export it in the shell that launches the app,
      and add it to the CUA_ENV object in electron/cua.mjs). Verify the
      "cua-driver vX is available" message no longer appears. Unverified that this
      variable works on macOS, so check.
   d. Packaged builds only: electron/updater.mjs startUpdater() checks GitHub 15s after
      launch and hourly. [ASK] me, then make it a no-op for this internal build.
      (It is already dormant for unpackaged `pnpm dev:desktop` runs.)
   e. Set WRANGLER_SEND_METRICS=false and NEXT_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1 in the shell.
   f. Search the repo (src, electron, server, shared, companion, scripts, index.html)
