4. INSTALL
   - `cd {INSTALL_DIR} && pnpm install` (corepack may fetch the repo-pinned pnpm).
   - Leave pnpm's ignored build scripts (core-js, workerd) blocked.
   - I may need to approve my corporate proxy or registry mirror. [ASK] if the install
     can't reach the npm registry or GitHub (Electron binary download).

5. DESKTOP BUILD
   - Read the "Package the desktop application" section of README.md and the
     package:mac / dev:desktop entries in package.json, then recommend ONE option:
       A) Run from source: three terminals (pnpm dev:server, pnpm dev, pnpm dev:desktop).
          Note dev:desktop first runs scripts/prepare-cloudflared.mjs, which downloads a
          pinned cloudflared binary from github.com/cloudflare/cloudflared. It does not
          start a tunnel. [ASK] before running it.
       B) Build a local unsigned app with `pnpm package:mac` (needs Xcode command line
          tools; Gatekeeper may block an unsigned app). [ASK] before running it.
   - Do NOT install the official prebuilt DMG from GitHub releases: it ships with
     PostHog analytics and the auto-updater enabled, and my patch would not apply.
   - Never run two harness servers at once (they share a data-dir lock).

6. macOS PERMISSIONS FOR "THIS COMPUTER" (local computer control)
   - macOS needs Screen Recording and Accessibility granted to the app, then quit and
     reopen it. I will grant them myself in System Settings; tell me when.
   - In source mode the server falls back to ~/Library/Application Support/openmausbot
     for the Cua connection file. Only set OMB_USER_DATA if the app reports
     "CUA Driver is not ready".

7. MODELS VIA LITELLM (NO LOCAL MODELS)
   - Ask me for: LiteLLM base URL {LITELLM_BASE_URL} (must be an internal
     org host ending in /v1), model alias {LITELLM_MODEL_NAME}, and the env-var name for
     the key. I will enter the key myself.
   - Add an instance to ~/.openmausbot/config.json under "instances" (back the file up
     first, merge don't overwrite):
       "litellm": {
         "driver": "openai-compat",
         "displayName": "Company LiteLLM",
         "environment": { "LITELLM_KEY": "<I will fill this in>" },
         "config": { "url": "{LITELLM_BASE_URL}", "apiKeyEnv": "LITELLM_KEY",
                     "model": "{LITELLM_MODEL_NAME}" }
       }
     (keys are stored in plaintext, mode 0600; use a key scoped to this use only.)
     Set config.tools=false only if the model has no tool support.
   - Restart the harness (instances are read at startup).
   - In the New Bot dialog, set the default model to this instance so no bot defaults to
     an external provider. Don't sign in to any other provider.

